# Class: obo:ACTAN_0000909 (young-calling ethotype)

AnnotationAssertion(oboInOwl:created_by obo:ACTAN_0000909 "Ditch Townsend")
AnnotationAssertion(oboInOwl:creation_date obo:ACTAN_0000909 "2025-10-26T15:58:12.843325Z")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(dc:date "1950"^^xsd:decimal) Annotation(dc:source "doi:10.1163/156853981X00220") oboInOwl:hasBroadSynonym obo:ACTAN_0000909 "calling movement")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(dc:contributor "https://orcid.org/0000-0002-4277-2151") Annotation(dc:source "doi:10.1163/156853981X00220") oboInOwl:hasDefinition obo:ACTAN_0000909 "Ethotype in which an adult draws in endangered young to itself as their protective cover.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(dc:date "1950"^^xsd:decimal) Annotation(dc:source "doi:10.1163/156853981X00220") Annotation(skos:scopeNote "\"Calling the young;\"") oboInOwl:hasExactSynonym obo:ACTAN_0000909 "young-calling"@en)
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(dc:date "1950"^^xsd:decimal) Annotation(dc:source "doi:10.1163/156853981X00220") oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym obo:ACTAN_0000909 "leading the young")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(dc:contributor "https://orcid.org/0000-0002-4277-2151") rdfs:label obo:ACTAN_0000909 "young-calling ethotype"@en)
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:seeAlso obo:ACTAN_0000909 obo:ACTAN_0000906)
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(dc:source "doi:10.1163/156853981X00220") skos:example obo:ACTAN_0000909 "\"Tilapia natalensis...
In case of some danger the female, after having made some violent movements against an eventual intruder... retreats towards the young and assumes a diagonal position, the longitudinal axis making an angle of about 10 or 20 [degrees] with the horizontal, the head lower than the tail. In this position she swims slowly backwards... the young move... closely along the body towards the mouth in which they actively penetrate or are passively taken up by the female.\"")
SubClassOf(obo:ACTAN_0000909 obo:ACTAN_0000118)
SubClassOf(obo:ACTAN_0000909 ObjectSomeValuesFrom(obo:BFO_0000055 obo:ACTAN_0000317))

# Class: obo:ACTAN_0000910 (bubble piping)

AnnotationAssertion(terms:conformsTo obo:ACTAN_0000910 <https://github.com/Active-Animals/Ontology/patterns/context_by_entity>)
AnnotationAssertion(oboInOwl:created_by obo:ACTAN_0000910 "Ditch Townsend")
AnnotationAssertion(oboInOwl:creation_date obo:ACTAN_0000910 "2025-11-06T17:54:41.77654Z")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(rdfs:isDefinedBy "doi:10.1242/jeb.198.1.79") Annotation(skos:scopeNote "\"These data show that during ASR with a buccal bubble present the trunk rests on the substratum while the head is either neutral or positively buoyant and held at the water surface.\"") oboInOwl:hasDefinition obo:ACTAN_0000910 "Piping in which the trunk rests on the substratum while, with a buccal bubble present, the head is held at the water surface.

The head may be either neutral or positively buoyant.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(dc:date "1995"^^xsd:decimal) Annotation(dc:source "doi:10.1242/jeb.198.1.79") Annotation(skos:scopeNote "\"...hydrostatic role for the buccal bubble.\"") oboInOwl:hasExactSynonym obo:ACTAN_0000910 "buccal bubble hydrostasis")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(dc:date "1995"^^xsd:decimal) Annotation(dc:source "doi:10.1242/jeb.198.1.79") Annotation(skos:scopeNote "\"...release their bubble...\"") oboInOwl:hasNarrowSynonym obo:ACTAN_0000910 "bubble releasing")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(dc:date "1995"^^xsd:decimal) Annotation(dc:source "doi:10.1242/jeb.198.1.79") oboInOwl:hasNarrowSynonym obo:ACTAN_0000910 "bubble-gulping"@en)
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(dc:date "1995"^^xsd:decimal) Annotation(dc:source "doi:10.1242/jeb.198.1.79") oboInOwl:hasNarrowSynonym obo:ACTAN_0000910 "bubble-holding")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(dc:contributor "https://orcid.org/0000-0002-4277-2151") rdfs:label obo:ACTAN_0000910 "bubble piping"@en)
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(dc:source "doi:10.1242/jeb.198.1.79") skos:scopeNote obo:ACTAN_0000910 "\"All bubble-gulping species possessed a negatively buoyant trunk, regardless of the presence of a swimbladder... lift derived from the swimbladder and the bubble act independently when the fish is performing ASR in the arched position. The bubble-gulping species P. olorum and Chlamydogobius, both of which lack a swimbladder, performed ASR (arched position) in a similar manner to those bubblegulping  species with a swimbladder. The non-bubble-gulping species F. tamarensis performed ASR when arched but used the beached position most frequently. All of the bubble-gulping species appeared to use bubble lift combined with the flexibility of the body to arch the head upwards, placing the mouth at the water surface. As a result, we considered lift and weight acting on the head to be independent from lift and weight acting on the trunk.\"")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(dc:source "doi:10.1242/jeb.198.1.79") skos:scopeNote obo:ACTAN_0000910 "\"Two obvious roles for the buccal bubble are to enhance ASR by further oxygenating the water prior to ventilating the gills and to provide O2 directly to respiratory tissues in the buccal cavity, as occurs in some gobies.\"")
SubClassOf(obo:ACTAN_0000910 obo:ACTAN_0000591)
SubClassOf(Annotation(dc:source "doi:10.1242/jeb.198.1.79") obo:ACTAN_0000910 ObjectSomeValuesFrom(obo:BFO_0000051 obo:ACTAN_0000668))
SubClassOf(obo:ACTAN_0000910 ObjectSomeValuesFrom(obo:RO_0000057 obo:UBERON_0000167))

# Class: obo:ACTAN_0000911 (beaching regime)

AnnotationAssertion(terms:conformsTo obo:ACTAN_0000911 <https://github.com/Active-Animals/Ontology/patterns/locomotion_realizing_regime>)
AnnotationAssertion(oboInOwl:created_by obo:ACTAN_0000911 "Ditch Townsend")
AnnotationAssertion(oboInOwl:creation_date obo:ACTAN_0000911 "2025-11-07T08:22:40.205691Z")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(dc:contributor "https://orcid.org/0000-0002-4277-2151") Annotation(dc:source "doi:10.1242/jeb.198.1.79") oboInOwl:hasDefinition obo:ACTAN_0000911 "Interfacing-regime in which the body is positioned partially on the substratum under water and partially emersed above water.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(dc:date "1995"^^xsd:decimal) Annotation(dc:source "doi:10.1242/jeb.198.1.79") oboInOwl:hasExactSynonym obo:ACTAN_0000911 "beaching"@en)
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(dc:contributor "https://orcid.org/0000-0002-4277-2151") rdfs:label obo:ACTAN_0000911 "beaching regime")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(dc:source "doi:10.1242/jeb.198.1.79") skos:scopeNote obo:ACTAN_0000911 "\"...intertidal benthic gobies performed ASR in shallow water... by beaching the body with the anterior dorsal surface emersed and the mouth just below the water surface...\"")
SubClassOf(obo:ACTAN_0000911 obo:ACTAN_0000086)
SubClassOf(obo:ACTAN_0000911 ObjectSomeValuesFrom(obo:BFO_0000051 obo:ACTAN_0000469))
SubClassOf(obo:ACTAN_0000911 ObjectSomeValuesFrom(obo:BFO_0000055 obo:ACTAN_0000183))
SubClassOf(obo:ACTAN_0000911 ObjectSomeValuesFrom(obo:BFO_0000055 obo:ACTAN_0000188))
SubClassOf(obo:ACTAN_0000911 ObjectSomeValuesFrom(obo:BFO_0000055 obo:ACTAN_0000543))
SubClassOf(obo:ACTAN_0000911 ObjectSomeValuesFrom(obo:BFO_0000055 obo:ACTAN_0000929))

# Class: obo:ACTAN_0000912 (tidying construction)

AnnotationAssertion(terms:conformsTo obo:ACTAN_0000912 <https://github.com/Active-Animals/Ontology/patterns/technical_by_kinetics>)
AnnotationAssertion(oboInOwl:created_by obo:ACTAN_0000912 "Ditch Townsend")
AnnotationAssertion(oboInOwl:creation_date obo:ACTAN_0000912 "2025-11-07T10:56:33.042225Z")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(rdfs:isDefinedBy "doi:10.1163/156853981X00220") Annotation(skos:scopeNote "\"The substrate is thoroughly cleaned by nipping off sand and detritus and carrying it away.\"") oboInOwl:hasDefinition obo:ACTAN_0000912 "Construction that cleans away detritus from a substrate.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(dc:date "2006"^^xsd:decimal) Annotation(dc:source "doi:10.1093/auk/123.4.967") oboInOwl:hasExactSynonym obo:ACTAN_0000912 "clearing")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(dc:date "2016"^^xsd:decimal) Annotation(dc:source "doi:10.3819/ccbr.2016.110005") oboInOwl:hasExactSynonym obo:ACTAN_0000912 "tidying"@en)
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(dc:date "1950"^^xsd:decimal) Annotation(dc:source "doi:10.1163/156853981X00220") oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym obo:ACTAN_0000912 "cleaning")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(dc:contributor "https://orcid.org/0000-0002-4277-2151") rdfs:label obo:ACTAN_0000912 "tidying construction"@en)
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(dc:source "doi:10.1163/156853981X00220") skos:example obo:ACTAN_0000912 "\"Hemichromis bimaculatus...
she usually lays eggs only on the spot cleaned before...\"")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(dc:source "doi:10.1093/auk/123.4.967") skos:example obo:ACTAN_0000912 "\"Parotia carolae...
Court clearing. — A male nondisplay court-preparation behavior. A range of activities in which leaves, leaf litter, or other forest debris are removed from the court floor.\"")
SubClassOf(obo:ACTAN_0000912 obo:ACTAN_0000272)
SubClassOf(obo:ACTAN_0000912 ObjectSomeValuesFrom(obo:BFO_0000051 obo:ACTAN_0000727))
SubClassOf(obo:ACTAN_0000912 ObjectSomeValuesFrom(obo:RO_0000057 obo:ENVO_00010483))

# Class: obo:ACTAN_0000913 (piling construction)

AnnotationAssertion(terms:conformsTo obo:ACTAN_0000913 <https://github.com/Active-Animals/Ontology/patterns/technical_by_kinetics>)
AnnotationAssertion(oboInOwl:created_by obo:ACTAN_0000913 "Ditch Townsend")
AnnotationAssertion(oboInOwl:creation_date obo:ACTAN_0000913 "2025-11-07T10:56:42.23654Z")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(dc:contributor "https://orcid.org/0000-0002-4277-2151") Annotation(dc:source "doi:10.1674/0003-0031(2000)144[0187:SBITBC]2.0.CO;2") Annotation(rdfs:comment "Termite and similar mounds are excluded, because they are structures which emerge from other constructing activities such as cementing. Our meaning predominantly involves the use of loose material.") oboInOwl:hasDefinition obo:ACTAN_0000913 "Construction that covers a space with a collection from the surrounding substrate.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(dc:date "2000"^^xsd:decimal) Annotation(dc:source "doi:10.1674/0003-0031(2000)144[0187:SBITBC]2.0.CO;2") oboInOwl:hasExactSynonym obo:ACTAN_0000913 "depositing")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(dc:date "1859"^^xsd:decimal) Annotation(dc:source "doi:10.5962/bhl.title.82303") oboInOwl:hasExactSynonym obo:ACTAN_0000913 "piling")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(dc:date "1926"^^xsd:decimal) Annotation(dc:source "doi:10.5962/p.203769") oboInOwl:hasNarrowSynonym obo:ACTAN_0000913 "burying")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(dc:date "2000"^^xsd:decimal) Annotation(dc:source "doi:10.1674/0003-0031(2000)144[0187:SBITBC]2.0.CO;2") oboInOwl:hasNarrowSynonym obo:ACTAN_0000913 "filling")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(dc:date "2015"^^xsd:decimal) Annotation(dc:source "doi:10.1007/s10071-014-0761-0") oboInOwl:hasNarrowSynonym obo:ACTAN_0000913 "masoning")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(dc:date "2000"^^xsd:decimal) Annotation(dc:source "doi:10.1674/0003-0031(2000)144[0187:SBITBC]2.0.CO;2") oboInOwl:hasNarrowSynonym obo:ACTAN_0000913 "mound-building")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(dc:date "2000"^^xsd:decimal) Annotation(dc:source "doi:10.1674/0003-0031(2000)144[0187:SBITBC]2.0.CO;2") oboInOwl:hasNarrowSynonym obo:ACTAN_0000913 "mounding"@en)
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(dc:date "2016"^^xsd:decimal) Annotation(dc:source "doi:10.3819/ccbr.2016.110005") oboInOwl:hasNarrowSynonym obo:ACTAN_0000913 "plating")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(dc:date "2015"^^xsd:decimal) Annotation(dc:source "doi:10.1007/s10071-014-0761-0") oboInOwl:hasNarrowSynonym obo:ACTAN_0000913 "walling")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(dc:date "2000"^^xsd:decimal) Annotation(dc:source "doi:10.1674/0003-0031(2000)144[0187:SBITBC]2.0.CO;2") oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym obo:ACTAN_0000913 "covering")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(dc:date "2000"^^xsd:decimal) Annotation(dc:source "doi:10.1674/0003-0031(2000)144[0187:SBITBC]2.0.CO;2") oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym obo:ACTAN_0000913 "nest-building")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(dc:contributor "https://orcid.org/0000-0002-4277-2151") rdfs:label obo:ACTAN_0000913 "piling construction")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(dc:source "doi:10.1146/annurev-ecolsys-102209-144712") skos:example obo:ACTAN_0000913 "\"Megapodes construct nest mounds from which the young emerge fully independent of adults, and these birds select mound sites with thick vegetative cover to prevent desiccation of the incubating eggs.\"")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(dc:source "doi:10.1674/0003-0031(2000)144[0187:SBITBC]2.0.CO;2") skos:example obo:ACTAN_0000913 "\"Nocomis Girard is a genus of nest-building chubs (Cyprinidae)...
...the male excavates a concavity which he fills with pebbles to form a platform...\"")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(dc:source "doi:10.1007/s10071-014-0761-0") skos:example obo:ACTAN_0000913 "\"The cutlips minnow collects around 300 identical pebbles and builds a mound 35 cm wide and 10 cm high, and tilefish make coral mounds up to 1 m high.\"")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(dc:source "doi:10.3819/ccbr.2016.110005") skos:scopeNote obo:ACTAN_0000913 "\"At the most ‘basic’ level, nest-building efforts may culminate in a seemingly haphazard arrangement of piledup materials, such that a mound or plate (located on or above the ground, respectively) of sticks and twigs provides birds with a nesting substrate...\"")
SubClassOf(obo:ACTAN_0000913 obo:ACTAN_0000272)
SubClassOf(obo:ACTAN_0000913 ObjectSomeValuesFrom(obo:BFO_0000051 obo:ACTAN_0000727))
SubClassOf(obo:ACTAN_0000913 ObjectSomeValuesFrom(obo:RO_0000057 obo:ENVO_00010483))

# Class: obo:ACTAN_0000914 (sheltering placing)

AnnotationAssertion(terms:conformsTo obo:ACTAN_0000914 <https://github.com/Active-Animals/Ontology/patterns/sub_activity_by_quality>)
AnnotationAssertion(oboInOwl:created_by obo:ACTAN_0000914 "Ditch Townsend")
AnnotationAssertion(oboInOwl:creation_date obo:ACTAN_0000914 "2025-11-07T13:15:01.429538Z")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(dc:contributor "https://orcid.org/0000-0002-4277-2151") Annotation(dc:source "doi:10.1007/s10071-014-0761-0") oboInOwl:hasDefinition obo:ACTAN_0000914 "Placing which enables time to be spent in safety.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(dc:date "2021"^^xsd:decimal) Annotation(dc:source "doi:10.1111/tops.12554") oboInOwl:hasExactSynonym obo:ACTAN_0000914 "place shelter"@en)
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(dc:date "2015"^^xsd:decimal) Annotation(dc:source "doi:10.1007/s10071-014-0761-0") oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym obo:ACTAN_0000914 "housing")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(dc:contributor "https://orcid.org/0000-0002-4277-2151") rdfs:label obo:ACTAN_0000914 "sheltering placing"@en)
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:seeAlso obo:ACTAN_0000914 obo:ACTAN_0000913)
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:seeAlso obo:ACTAN_0000914 <https://github.com/Active-Animals/Ontology/ACTAN_0000377>)
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(dc:source "doi:10.1007/s10071-014-0761-0") skos:example obo:ACTAN_0000914 "\"The jawfish gathers together small rocks from the sand floor to build a wall in front of its burrow. These fishy masons search meticulously for rocks that fit together like a puzzle and leave a hole just big enough for it to slip through. Perhaps the most impressive builder is the rockmover wrasse. Each night it gathers up large bits of coral to make a house, in which it spends the night sleeping and abandons the next morning.\"")
SubClassOf(obo:ACTAN_0000914 obo:ACTAN_0000395)
SubClassOf(obo:ACTAN_0000914 ObjectSomeValuesFrom(obo:RO_0000086 obo:PATO_0002508))

# Class: obo:ACTAN_0000915 (thermoregulation placing)

AnnotationAssertion(terms:conformsTo obo:ACTAN_0000915 <https://github.com/Active-Animals/Ontology/patterns/sub_activity_by_quality>)
AnnotationAssertion(oboInOwl:created_by obo:ACTAN_0000915 "Ditch Townsend")
AnnotationAssertion(oboInOwl:creation_date obo:ACTAN_0000915 "2025-11-07T13:15:52.680542Z")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(dc:contributor "https://orcid.org/0000-0002-4277-2151") Annotation(rdfs:comment "doi:10.1146/annurev-ecolsys-102209-144712") oboInOwl:hasDefinition obo:ACTAN_0000915 "Placing which keeps temperatures suitable.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(dc:date "2021"^^xsd:decimal) Annotation(dc:source "doi:10.1111/tops.12554") oboInOwl:hasExactSynonym obo:ACTAN_0000915 "place thermo"@en)
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(dc:contributor "https://orcid.org/0000-0002-4277-2151") rdfs:label obo:ACTAN_0000915 "thermoregulation placing"@en)
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(dc:source "doi:10.1146/annurev-ecolsys-102209-144712") skos:example obo:ACTAN_0000915 "\"Crocodilians have a particularly restricted range of suitable incubation temperatures, and offspring survival is low in areas that lack sufficient open, sunny sites for nest mound construction.\"")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(dc:source "doi:10.1146/annurev-ecolsys-102209-144712") skos:example obo:ACTAN_0000915 "\"Megapodes construct nest mounds from which the young emerge fully independent of adults, and these birds select mound sites with thick vegetative cover to prevent desiccation of the incubating eggs.\"")
SubClassOf(obo:ACTAN_0000915 obo:ACTAN_0000395)
SubClassOf(obo:ACTAN_0000915 ObjectSomeValuesFrom(obo:RO_0000086 obo:PATO_0000146))

# Class: obo:ACTAN_0000916 (burial incubation)

AnnotationAssertion(terms:conformsTo obo:ACTAN_0000916 <https://github.com/Active-Animals/Ontology/patterns/context_by_activity>)
AnnotationAssertion(oboInOwl:created_by obo:ACTAN_0000916 "Ditch Townsend")
AnnotationAssertion(oboInOwl:creation_date obo:ACTAN_0000916 "2025-11-10T12:06:10.818231Z")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(dc:contributor "https://orcid.org/0000-0002-4277-2151") Annotation(dc:source "doi:10.1674/0003-0031(2000)144[0187:SBITBC]2.0.CO;2") oboInOwl:hasDefinition obo:ACTAN_0000916 "Incubation that covers eggs.

This may  improve embryonic homeostasis and reduce predation.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(dc:date "2000"^^xsd:decimal) Annotation(dc:source "doi:10.1674/0003-0031(2000)144[0187:SBITBC]2.0.CO;2") oboInOwl:hasExactSynonym obo:ACTAN_0000916 "burial"@en)
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(dc:contributor "https://orcid.org/0000-0002-4277-2151") rdfs:label obo:ACTAN_0000916 "burial incubation"@en)
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(dc:source "doi:10.1674/0003-0031(2000)144[0187:SBITBC]2.0.CO;2") skos:example obo:ACTAN_0000916 "\"After a number of spawns a male N leptocephalus covers the pit with pebbles and excavates another pit for spawning... Eggs become buried and are thought to receive a constant circulation of water and remain well aerated in the clean interstices of the nest.\"")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(dc:source "doi:10.1146/annurev-ecolsys-102209-144712") skos:example obo:ACTAN_0000916 "\"Crocodilians have a particularly restricted range of suitable incubation temperatures, and offspring survival is low in areas that lack sufficient open, sunny sites for nest mound construction.\"")
SubClassOf(obo:ACTAN_0000916 obo:ACTAN_0000474)
SubClassOf(obo:ACTAN_0000916 ObjectSomeValuesFrom(obo:BFO_0000051 obo:ACTAN_0000913))

# Class: obo:ACTAN_0000917 (association incubation)

AnnotationAssertion(terms:conformsTo obo:ACTAN_0000917 <https://github.com/Active-Animals/Ontology/patterns/context_composite>)
AnnotationAssertion(oboInOwl:created_by obo:ACTAN_0000917 "Ditch Townsend")
AnnotationAssertion(oboInOwl:creation_date obo:ACTAN_0000917 "2025-11-10T13:26:32.600227Z")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(dc:contributor "https://orcid.org/0000-0002-4277-2151") Annotation(dc:source "doi:10.1674/0003-0031(2000)144[0187:SBITBC]2.0.CO;2") oboInOwl:hasDefinition obo:ACTAN_0000917 "Incubation that symbiotically uses a host's nest.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(dc:date "2000"^^xsd:decimal) Annotation(dc:source "doi:10.1674/0003-0031(2000)144[0187:SBITBC]2.0.CO;2") oboInOwl:hasExactSynonym obo:ACTAN_0000917 "nest association"@en)
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(dc:contributor "https://orcid.org/0000-0002-4277-2151") rdfs:label obo:ACTAN_0000917 "association incubation")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(dc:source "doi:10.1674/0003-0031(2000)144[0187:SBITBC]2.0.CO;2") skos:example obo:ACTAN_0000917 "\"Other species of minnows, referred to as nest associates, often school and may spawn over active nests of Nocomis without contributing to the nest’s construction. Twenty-seven minnow species are reported as nest associates of Nocomis. Interaction of host and nest associate is thought to be mutualistic. Eggs and larvae of associates benefit from the parental care of nesting chub, and offspring of both host and associate may benefit from a dilution effect whereby predation risk per egg is reduced in the nest.\"")
SubClassOf(obo:ACTAN_0000917 obo:ACTAN_0000474)
SubClassOf(obo:ACTAN_0000917 ObjectSomeValuesFrom(obo:BFO_0000051 obo:ACTAN_0000463))

# Class: obo:ACTAN_0000918 (tail quiver)

AnnotationAssertion(terms:conformsTo obo:ACTAN_0000918 <https://github.com/Active-Animals/Ontology/patterns/sub_activity_by_entity>)
AnnotationAssertion(oboInOwl:created_by obo:ACTAN_0000918 "Ditch Townsend")
AnnotationAssertion(oboInOwl:creation_date obo:ACTAN_0000918 "2025-11-10T19:56:44.412031Z")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(rdfs:isDefinedBy "doi:10.2307/4083155") Annotation(skos:scopeNote "\"Presence of tail quivering suggests possible relationship among corvids, estrildines, and ploceids.\"") oboInOwl:hasDefinition obo:ACTAN_0000918 "Quiver that involves the tail.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(dc:date "1966"^^xsd:decimal) Annotation(dc:source "doi:10.2307/4083155") oboInOwl:hasExactSynonym obo:ACTAN_0000918 "tail quivering"@en)
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(dc:contributor "https://orcid.org/0000-0002-4277-2151") rdfs:label obo:ACTAN_0000918 "tail quiver"@en)
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(dc:source "doi:10.1674/0003-0031(2000)144[0187:SBITBC]2.0.CO;2") skos:example obo:ACTAN_0000918 "\"As the female chub initiated her run with tail quivering, the stoneroller darted towards her...\"")
SubClassOf(obo:ACTAN_0000918 obo:ACTAN_0000429)
SubClassOf(obo:ACTAN_0000918 ObjectSomeValuesFrom(obo:RO_0000057 obo:UBERON_0002415))

# Class: obo:ACTAN_0000919 (anal-fin flutter)

AnnotationAssertion(terms:conformsTo obo:ACTAN_0000919 <https://github.com/Active-Animals/Ontology/patterns/sub_activity_by_entity>)
AnnotationAssertion(oboInOwl:created_by obo:ACTAN_0000919 "Ditch Townsend")
AnnotationAssertion(oboInOwl:creation_date obo:ACTAN_0000919 "2025-11-10T20:17:14.669789Z")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(rdfs:isDefinedBy "doi:10.1674/0003-0031(2000)144[0187:SBITBC]2.0.CO;2") Annotation(skos:scopeNote "\"As he deposited the pebble upstream he vibrated his extended anal fin in the pit for up to 2 s (anal-fin fanning).\"") oboInOwl:hasDefinition obo:ACTAN_0000919 "Flutter that involves the anal fin.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(dc:date "2000"^^xsd:decimal) Annotation(dc:source "doi:10.1674/0003-0031(2000)144[0187:SBITBC]2.0.CO;2") oboInOwl:hasExactSynonym obo:ACTAN_0000919 "anal-fin-fanning"@en)
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(dc:contributor "https://orcid.org/0000-0002-4277-2151") rdfs:label obo:ACTAN_0000919 "anal-fin flutter"@en)
SubClassOf(obo:ACTAN_0000919 obo:ACTAN_0000851)
SubClassOf(obo:ACTAN_0000919 ObjectSomeValuesFrom(obo:RO_0000057 obo:UBERON_4000163))

# Class: obo:ACTAN_0000920 (solicitation courtship)

AnnotationAssertion(terms:conformsTo obo:ACTAN_0000920 <https://github.com/Active-Animals/Ontology/patterns/context_by_realization>)
AnnotationAssertion(oboInOwl:created_by obo:ACTAN_0000920 "Ditch Townsend")
AnnotationAssertion(oboInOwl:creation_date obo:ACTAN_0000920 "2024-12-28T21:26:16.841819Z")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(dc:contributor "https://orcid.org/0000-0002-4277-2151") Annotation(dc:source "doi:10.1163/156853981X00220") oboInOwl:hasDefinition obo:ACTAN_0000920 "Courtship in which an animal coaxes another to join in to begin gamete release.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(dc:date "1967"^^xsd:decimal) Annotation(dc:source "https://open.uct.ac.za/handle/11427/13101") oboInOwl:hasExactSynonym obo:ACTAN_0000920 "soliciting")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(dc:date "1999"^^xsd:decimal) Annotation(dc:source "doi:10.1537/ase.107.141") oboInOwl:hasNarrowSynonym obo:ACTAN_0000920 "copulatory solicitation")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(dc:date "1966"^^xsd:decimal) Annotation(dc:source "doi:10.2307/4083155") oboInOwl:hasNarrowSynonym obo:ACTAN_0000920 "precopulatory display"@en)
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(dc:date "2000"^^xsd:decimal) Annotation(dc:source "doi:10.1674/0003-0031(2000)144[0187:SBITBC]2.0.CO;2") oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym obo:ACTAN_0000920 "approach")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(dc:date "1950"^^xsd:decimal) Annotation(dc:source "doi:10.1163/156853981X00220") oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym obo:ACTAN_0000920 "coaxing")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(dc:date "2010"^^xsd:decimal) Annotation(dc:source "doi:10.1007/s00265-010-0980-6") oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym obo:ACTAN_0000920 "gliding")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(dc:date "1950"^^xsd:decimal) Annotation(dc:source "doi:10.1163/156853981X00220") oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym obo:ACTAN_0000920 "invitation")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(dc:date "2000"^^xsd:decimal) Annotation(dc:source "doi:10.1674/0003-0031(2000)144[0187:SBITBC]2.0.CO;2") oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym obo:ACTAN_0000920 "posturing"@en)
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(dc:contributor "https://orcid.org/0000-0002-4277-2151") rdfs:label obo:ACTAN_0000920 "solicitation courtship")
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:seeAlso obo:ACTAN_0000920 obo:ACTAN_0000177)
AnnotationAssertion(skos:closeMatch obo:ACTAN_0000920 "NBO:0020241")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(dc:source "doi:10.1007/s00265-010-0980-6") skos:example obo:ACTAN_0000920 "\"...guppies (Poecilia reticulata)...

...the female ‘glided’, that is, when she swam towards the displaying male using her pectoral fins with a smooth motion; the more courtship a female receives, the more likely the female will glide.\"")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(dc:source "doi:10.1537/ase.107.141") skos:example obo:ACTAN_0000920 "\"Chimpanzee...
At Mahale, some estrous females approach and touch males on the shoulder, and so on, to solicit copulation.\"")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(dc:source "doi:10.1537/ase.107.141") skos:example obo:ACTAN_0000920 "\"Chimpanzee...
Goodall's Male invite: \"The male sits with thighs splayed and penile erection, looking toward a female in estrus. Sometimes his hair is erect...\" Male  courtship display pattern.\"")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(dc:source "doi:10.1674/0003-0031(2000)144[0187:SBITBC]2.0.CO;2") skos:example obo:ACTAN_0000920 "\"Nocomis leptocephalus...
Head facing upstream, the male hovered 2—4 cm above the pit floor. His dorsal and paired fins remained fully extended and his head was angled slightly downwards such that his body nearly paralleled the nest’s upstream slope. Successful spawning sequences always began with the pit-postured male.\"")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(dc:source "doi:10.1163/156853981X00220") skos:example obo:ACTAN_0000920 "\"Tilapia natalensis and T. nilotica...
The male swims slowly in front of the partner in the direction of his pit, always trying to show it a flank. If the partner stops, the male stops too and by swimming in front of the head of the partner he tries to coax it along again.\"\"")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(dc:source "doi:10.1089/zeb.2012.0861") skos:example obo:ACTAN_0000920 "\"Zebrafish...
Lead (leading): Returning at least three times to one location...; performed by females during courtship.\"")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(dc:source "doi:10.1089/zeb.2012.0861") skos:example obo:ACTAN_0000920 "\"Zebrafish...
Present (presenting): Halting and exposing side in front of a male or swimming up and down in front of male; performed by females during courtship.\"")
SubClassOf(obo:ACTAN_0000920 obo:ACTAN_0000472)
SubClassOf(obo:ACTAN_0000920 ObjectSomeValuesFrom(obo:BFO_0000055 obo:ACTAN_0000893))

# Class: obo:ACTAN_0000921 (jostle interference)

AnnotationAssertion(terms:conformsTo obo:ACTAN_0000921 <https://github.com/Active-Animals/Ontology/patterns/context_composite>)
AnnotationAssertion(oboInOwl:created_by obo:ACTAN_0000921 "Ditch Townsend")
AnnotationAssertion(oboInOwl:creation_date obo:ACTAN_0000921 "2025-11-11T12:06:16.843036Z")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(dc:contributor "https://orcid.org/0000-0002-4277-2151") Annotation(dc:source "doi:10.1674/0003-0031(2000)144[0187:SBITBC]2.0.CO;2") oboInOwl:hasDefinition obo:ACTAN_0000921 "Interference that involves active displacement from a preferred place.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(dc:date "2000"^^xsd:decimal) Annotation(dc:source "doi:10.1674/0003-0031(2000)144[0187:SBITBC]2.0.CO;2") oboInOwl:hasExactSynonym obo:ACTAN_0000921 "jockeying"@en)
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(dc:date "1859"^^xsd:decimal) Annotation(dc:source "doi:10.5962/bhl.title.82303") oboInOwl:hasExactSynonym obo:ACTAN_0000921 "jostling")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(dc:contributor "https://orcid.org/0000-0002-4277-2151") rdfs:label obo:ACTAN_0000921 "jostle interference")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(dc:source "doi:10.1674/0003-0031(2000)144[0187:SBITBC]2.0.CO;2") skos:example obo:ACTAN_0000921 "\"About ten female Nocomis leptocephalus actively jockeyed for a position over the rear slope of the nest from which they might begin their approach.\"")
SubClassOf(obo:ACTAN_0000921 obo:ACTAN_0000388)
SubClassOf(obo:ACTAN_0000921 ObjectSomeValuesFrom(obo:BFO_0000051 obo:ACTAN_0000930))

# Class: obo:ACTAN_0000922 (alignment relativity)

AnnotationAssertion(terms:conformsTo obo:ACTAN_0000922 <https://github.com/Active-Animals/Ontology/patterns/context_by_quality>)
AnnotationAssertion(oboInOwl:created_by obo:ACTAN_0000922 "Ditch Townsend")
AnnotationAssertion(oboInOwl:creation_date obo:ACTAN_0000922 "2025-11-12T08:31:02.945709Z")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(dc:contributor "https://orcid.org/0000-0002-4277-2151") Annotation(dc:source "doi:10.1674/0003-0031(2000)144[0187:SBITBC]2.0.CO;2") oboInOwl:hasDefinition obo:ACTAN_0000922 "Relativity that involves an animal positioning themself at a constant angle to another entity.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(dc:date "2000"^^xsd:decimal) Annotation(dc:source "doi:10.1674/0003-0031(2000)144[0187:SBITBC]2.0.CO;2") oboInOwl:hasExactSynonym obo:ACTAN_0000922 "alignment")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(dc:date "2000"^^xsd:decimal) Annotation(dc:source "doi:10.1674/0003-0031(2000)144[0187:SBITBC]2.0.CO;2") oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym obo:ACTAN_0000922 "angling"@en)
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(dc:contributor "https://orcid.org/0000-0002-4277-2151") rdfs:label obo:ACTAN_0000922 "alignment relativity")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(dc:source "doi:10.1674/0003-0031(2000)144[0187:SBITBC]2.0.CO;2") skos:example obo:ACTAN_0000922 "\"Nocomis leptocephalus...
Alignment. The female... stationed herself beneath the male with her snout directly below or slightly ahead of his extended pectoral fins. Her body aligned parallel to the pit’s long axis.... She either remained posted beneath the male for a few seconds or immediately initiated the spawning run. During alignment the male tilted the dorsal half of his body to one side as the female’s snout moved beneath his pectoral region. The female’s movement into the pit determined the direction of his sagittal tilt. If she sidled into the pit his dorsal surface tilted towards her entry; if she moved into the pit directly beneath his tail he might angle his body in either direction based on her final position.\"")
SubClassOf(obo:ACTAN_0000922 obo:ACTAN_0000288)
SubClassOf(obo:ACTAN_0000922 ObjectSomeValuesFrom(obo:RO_0000086 obo:PATO_0001653))

# Class: obo:ACTAN_0000923 (pelagic spawning)

AnnotationAssertion(terms:conformsTo obo:ACTAN_0000923 <https://github.com/Active-Animals/Ontology/patterns/context_by_entity>)
AnnotationAssertion(oboInOwl:created_by obo:ACTAN_0000923 "Ditch Townsend")
AnnotationAssertion(oboInOwl:creation_date obo:ACTAN_0000923 "2025-11-12T12:25:18.533324Z")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(rdfs:isDefinedBy "doi:10.1007/BF01609520") Annotation(skos:scopeNote "\"A temporary spawning ascent into the water column is a nearly universal phenomenon among reef fishes spawning pelagic eggs.\"") oboInOwl:hasDefinition obo:ACTAN_0000923 "Spawning which is in the water column.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(dc:date "1973"^^xsd:decimal) Annotation(dc:source "doi:10.1007/BF01609520") Annotation(skos:scopeNote "\"...pelagic eggs to be released...\"") oboInOwl:hasExactSynonym obo:ACTAN_0000923 "pelagic release")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(dc:date "1973"^^xsd:decimal) Annotation(dc:source "doi:10.1007/BF01609520") Annotation(skos:scopeNote "\"...spawning pelagic eggs.\"") rdfs:label obo:ACTAN_0000923 "pelagic spawning")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(dc:source "doi:10.11369/jji1950.34.76") skos:scopeNote obo:ACTAN_0000923 "\"A temporary spawning ascent into the water column is a nearly universal phenomenon among reef fishes spawning pelagic eggs. This behavioral pattern is usually referred to as the \"spawning rush\", although in some species, e.g. ostraciids and pomacanthids, such ascents are extremely slow.\"")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(dc:source "doi:10.1674/0003-0031(2000)144[0187:SBITBC]2.0.CO;2") skos:scopeNote obo:ACTAN_0000923 "\"Nocomis leptocephalus...
A successful spawning run always was initiated by the female. With her body pressed to the substrate, she quickly swam about 3—5 cm upstream while quivering her tail and caudal peduncle. The male remained tilted as he promptly accompanied her short run with rapid tail beats. As the female moved forward over the upstream rim of the pit, she gaped and abruptly tossed her head vertically into the water column.\"")
SubClassOf(obo:ACTAN_0000923 obo:ACTAN_0000475)
SubClassOf(obo:ACTAN_0000923 ObjectSomeValuesFrom(obo:BFO_0000051 obo:ACTAN_0000659))
SubClassOf(obo:ACTAN_0000923 ObjectSomeValuesFrom(obo:RO_0000057 obo:ENVO_06105011))

# Class: obo:ACTAN_0000924 (accompanying relativity)

AnnotationAssertion(terms:conformsTo obo:ACTAN_0000924 <https://github.com/Active-Animals/Ontology/patterns/context_by_quality>)
AnnotationAssertion(oboInOwl:created_by obo:ACTAN_0000924 "Ditch Townsend")
AnnotationAssertion(oboInOwl:creation_date obo:ACTAN_0000924 "2025-11-12T20:50:31.147358Z")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(dc:contributor "https://orcid.org/0000-0002-4277-2151") Annotation(dc:source "doi:10.1674/0003-0031(2000)144[0187:SBITBC]2.0.CO;2") oboInOwl:hasDefinition obo:ACTAN_0000924 "Relativity that involves close, ongoing interaction.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(dc:date "2000"^^xsd:decimal) Annotation(dc:source "doi:10.1674/0003-0031(2000)144[0187:SBITBC]2.0.CO;2") oboInOwl:hasExactSynonym obo:ACTAN_0000924 "accompanying"@en)
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(dc:date "2013"^^xsd:decimal) Annotation(dc:source "doi:10.1089/zeb.2012.0861") oboInOwl:hasExactSynonym obo:ACTAN_0000924 "escorting"@en)
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(dc:contributor "https://orcid.org/0000-0002-4277-2151") rdfs:label obo:ACTAN_0000924 "accompanying relativity"@en)
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(dc:source "doi:10.1674/0003-0031(2000)144[0187:SBITBC]2.0.CO;2") skos:example obo:ACTAN_0000924 "\"...a small tuberculate male Campostoma anomalum (stoneroller)... accompanied nine separate spawning runs, disrupting six. As the female chub initiated her run with tail quivering, the stoneroller darted towards her and became appressed to her flank opposite the male chub.\"")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(dc:source "ISBN:9780980857252") skos:scopeNote obo:ACTAN_0000924 "\"...as follower, species do not only interact, but also accompany the nuclear species during a determined period of time...\"")
SubClassOf(obo:ACTAN_0000924 obo:ACTAN_0000288)
SubClassOf(obo:ACTAN_0000924 ObjectSomeValuesFrom(obo:RO_0000086 obo:PATO_0002259))

# Class: obo:ACTAN_0000925 (contacting movement)

AnnotationAssertion(terms:conformsTo obo:ACTAN_0000925 <https://github.com/Active-Animals/Ontology/patterns/movement>)
AnnotationAssertion(oboInOwl:created_by obo:ACTAN_0000925 "Ditch Townsend")
AnnotationAssertion(oboInOwl:creation_date obo:ACTAN_0000925 "2025-11-16T11:40:06.767597Z")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(dc:contributor "https://orcid.org/0000-0002-4277-2151") Annotation(dc:source "ISBN:9781482294347") oboInOwl:hasDefinition obo:ACTAN_0000925 "Movement in which a surface becomes apposed to another.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(dc:date "2000"^^xsd:decimal) Annotation(dc:source "doi:10.1674/0003-0031(2000)144[0187:SBITBC]2.0.CO;2") oboInOwl:hasExactSynonym obo:ACTAN_0000925 "apposing"@en)
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(dc:date "1859"^^xsd:decimal) Annotation(dc:source "doi:10.5962/bhl.title.82303") oboInOwl:hasExactSynonym obo:ACTAN_0000925 "contact")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(dc:contributor "https://orcid.org/0000-0002-4277-2151") rdfs:label obo:ACTAN_0000925 "contacting movement")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(dc:source "doi:10.1674/0003-0031(2000)144[0187:SBITBC]2.0.CO;2") skos:example obo:ACTAN_0000925 "\"Nocomis leptocephalus...
As her snout approached vertical she rolled the anterior portion of her body away from the male placing her dorsum in contact with his anterior flank.\"")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(dc:source "doi:10.1674/0003-0031(2000)144[0187:SBITBC]2.0.CO;2") skos:example obo:ACTAN_0000925 "\"Nocomis leptocephalus...
Her snout traversed a 45[degree] arc as the side of her head apposed either the male’s operculum or his anterior flank just above the pectoral fin.\"")
SubClassOf(obo:ACTAN_0000925 obo:ACTAN_0000082)
SubClassOf(obo:ACTAN_0000925 ObjectSomeValuesFrom(obo:RO_0000086 obo:PATO_0001961))

# Class: obo:ACTAN_0000926 (clasp grip)

AnnotationAssertion(terms:conformsTo obo:ACTAN_0000926 <https://github.com/Active-Animals/Ontology/patterns/sub_activity_by_quality>)
AnnotationAssertion(oboInOwl:created_by obo:ACTAN_0000926 "Ditch Townsend")
AnnotationAssertion(oboInOwl:creation_date obo:ACTAN_0000926 "2025-11-16T21:32:45.296989Z")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(dc:contributor "https://orcid.org/0000-0002-4277-2151") Annotation(dc:source "doi:10.1674/0003-0031(2000)144[0187:SBITBC]2.0.CO;2") oboInOwl:hasDefinition obo:ACTAN_0000926 "Grip which uses a recurved body part.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(dc:date "1999"^^xsd:decimal) Annotation(dc:source "doi:10.1537/ase.107.141") oboInOwl:hasExactSynonym obo:ACTAN_0000926 "clasp")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(dc:date "1979"^^xsd:decimal) Annotation(dc:source "https://www.jstor.org/stable/986582") oboInOwl:hasExactSynonym obo:ACTAN_0000926 "clasping"@en)
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(dc:date "1859"^^xsd:decimal) Annotation(dc:source "doi:10.5962/bhl.title.82303") oboInOwl:hasExactSynonym obo:ACTAN_0000926 "prehension")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(dc:date "2000"^^xsd:decimal) Annotation(dc:source "doi:10.1674/0003-0031(2000)144[0187:SBITBC]2.0.CO;2") oboInOwl:hasNarrowSynonym obo:ACTAN_0000926 "spawning clasp")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(dc:contributor "https://orcid.org/0000-0002-4277-2151") rdfs:label obo:ACTAN_0000926 "clasp grip")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(dc:source "doi:10.1537/ase.107.141") skos:example obo:ACTAN_0000926 "\"Chimpanzees...
\"\"Sit or lie with arms tightly clasped around self...\" Observed at Gombe as \"in a relaxed manner during resting.\"\"")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(dc:source "doi:10.1674/0003-0031(2000)144[0187:SBITBC]2.0.CO;2") skos:example obo:ACTAN_0000926 "\"Nocomis leptocephalus...
His anterior body (from snout to anal fin) contracted into a semicircle and resembled a horseshoe about the vertically arched female. Facing away from the clasp, the female’s abdominal region was compressed laterally as the male constricted his body.\"")
SubClassOf(obo:ACTAN_0000926 obo:ACTAN_0000628)
SubClassOf(obo:ACTAN_0000926 ObjectSomeValuesFrom(obo:RO_0000086 obo:PATO_0002211))

# Class: obo:ACTAN_0000927 (dissociation relativity)

AnnotationAssertion(terms:conformsTo obo:ACTAN_0000927 <https://github.com/Active-Animals/Ontology/patterns/context_by_quality>)
AnnotationAssertion(oboInOwl:created_by obo:ACTAN_0000927 "Ditch Townsend")
AnnotationAssertion(oboInOwl:creation_date obo:ACTAN_0000927 "2025-11-17T11:54:03.234156Z")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(dc:date "1950"^^xsd:decimal) Annotation(dc:source "doi:10.1163/156853981X00220") oboInOwl:hasBroadSynonym obo:ACTAN_0000927 "separating")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(dc:contributor "https://orcid.org/0000-0002-4277-2151") Annotation(dc:source "doi:10.1674/0003-0031(2000)144[0187:SBITBC]2.0.CO;2") oboInOwl:hasDefinition obo:ACTAN_0000927 "Relativity in which one separates from another.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(dc:date "2000"^^xsd:decimal) Annotation(dc:source "doi:10.1674/0003-0031(2000)144[0187:SBITBC]2.0.CO;2") oboInOwl:hasExactSynonym obo:ACTAN_0000927 "dissociation"@en)
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(dc:contributor "https://orcid.org/0000-0002-4277-2151") rdfs:label obo:ACTAN_0000927 "dissociation relativity")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(dc:source "doi:10.1111/j.1469-185X.2007.00029.x") skos:example obo:ACTAN_0000927 "\"Apterygote insects transfer sperm indirectly via spermatophores or sperm drops. Spermatophores are usually deposited on the ground or on special silk threads. They are then picked up by the female, sometimes with active male participation and close physical contact between male and female, sometimes in dissociation.\"")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(dc:source "doi:10.1674/0003-0031(2000)144[0187:SBITBC]2.0.CO;2") skos:example obo:ACTAN_0000927 "\"Nocomis leptocephalus...
Dissociation. The spawning clasp was completed in about a second and the pair immediately separated.\"")
SubClassOf(obo:ACTAN_0000927 obo:ACTAN_0000288)
SubClassOf(obo:ACTAN_0000927 ObjectSomeValuesFrom(obo:RO_0000086 obo:PATO_0002233))

# Class: obo:ACTAN_0000928 (failure switch)

AnnotationAssertion(terms:conformsTo obo:ACTAN_0000928 <https://github.com/Active-Animals/Ontology/patterns/disposition_by_quality>)
AnnotationAssertion(oboInOwl:created_by obo:ACTAN_0000928 "Ditch Townsend")
AnnotationAssertion(oboInOwl:creation_date obo:ACTAN_0000928 "2025-11-17T17:59:25.882901Z")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(dc:contributor "https://orcid.org/0000-0002-4277-2151") Annotation(dc:source "doi:10.1674/0003-0031(2000)144[0187:SBITBC]2.0.CO;2") oboInOwl:hasDefinition obo:ACTAN_0000928 "Switch which follows a behaviour disruption.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(dc:date "1987"^^xsd:decimal) Annotation(dc:source "doi:10.11369/jji1950.34.76") oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym obo:ACTAN_0000928 "failure"@en)
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(dc:date "2005"^^xsd:decimal) Annotation(dc:source "doi:10.1017/S1464793104006700") oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym obo:ACTAN_0000928 "flubbing")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(dc:contributor "https://orcid.org/0000-0002-4277-2151") rdfs:label obo:ACTAN_0000928 "failure switch"@en)
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(dc:source "doi:10.1371/journal.pone.0083116") skos:example obo:ACTAN_0000928 "\"...Southeast Asian olive frog, Rana adenopleura...
Attacks by unpaired males were highly successful in disrupting mating by amplectant pairs causing mating failure.\"")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(dc:source "https://open.uct.ac.za/handle/11427/13101") skos:example obo:ACTAN_0000928 "\"Ardeola ibis...
Head Flick...
Immediately after threatening but failing to dislodge a trespasser.\"")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(dc:source "doi:10.1674/0003-0031(2000)144[0187:SBITBC]2.0.CO;2") skos:example obo:ACTAN_0000928 "\"Nocomis leptocephalus...
Disruption of an interim male or spawning sequence resulted from aggressive interactions with conspecific males, nest associates and egg or fish predators. Disruption of a spawning sequence also resulted if a male or female responded inappropriately to their mate. For example, alignment failed if a female retreated or was displaced from the spawning pit prior to her run. Runs infrequently were disrupted when a female failed to retroflex and exited the pit over the upstream slope.\"")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(dc:source "doi:10.1017/S1464793104006700") skos:scopeNote obo:ACTAN_0000928 "\"Another stimulus might stem from the precision of male movements, i.e. from the ‘flubs’, or unsuccessful intromission attempts by males. Such flubs are common in spiders, and if they reflect the male’s competency in copulation, females are predicted to be under selection to use the flub to hit ratio as a criterion in cryptic female choice.\"")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(dc:source "doi:10.5962/bhl.title.82303") skos:scopeNote obo:ACTAN_0000928 "\"Now let us suppose that the ancient progenitor of our European cuckoo had the habits of the American cuckoo; but that occasionally she laid an egg in another bird’s nest. If the old bird profited by this occasional habit, or if the young were made more vigorous by advantage having been taken of the mistaken maternal instinct of another bird, than by their own mother’s care, encumbered as she can hardly fail to be by having eggs and young of different ages at the same time; then the old birds or the fostered young would gain an advantage.\"")
SubClassOf(obo:ACTAN_0000928 obo:ACTAN_0000541)
SubClassOf(obo:ACTAN_0000928 ObjectSomeValuesFrom(obo:RO_0000086 obo:PATO_0001507))

# Class: obo:ACTAN_0000929 (dynamically-unstable pattern)

AnnotationAssertion(terms:conformsTo obo:ACTAN_0000929 <https://github.com/Active-Animals/Ontology/patterns/disposition_by_quality>)
AnnotationAssertion(oboInOwl:created_by obo:ACTAN_0000929 "Ditch Townsend")
AnnotationAssertion(oboInOwl:creation_date obo:ACTAN_0000929 "2025-11-17T18:00:09.38796Z")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(rdfs:isDefinedBy "doi:10.1371/journal.pcbi.1002915") Annotation(skos:scopeNote "\"Perturbations, such as disruption induced by predator attacks, or more generally, sources of intrinsic or extrinsic noise, can cause the system to leave its existing dynamically stable state and enter an unstable transitional regime. Depending on the degree and type of perturbation the group may find itself either drawn back towards the previous state, or if perturbed sufficiently far, to be drawn into the alternative dynamically-stable state.\"") oboInOwl:hasDefinition obo:ACTAN_0000929 "Regime pattern which is transitional, between previous and future stable states.

The future may represent a return or an alternative.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(dc:date "2013"^^xsd:decimal) Annotation(dc:source "doi:10.1371/journal.pcbi.1002915") Annotation(skos:scopeNote "\"...dynamically stable state and enter an unstable transitional regime.\"") oboInOwl:hasExactSynonym obo:ACTAN_0000929 "dynamically unstable transitional regime")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(dc:date "2000"^^xsd:decimal) Annotation(dc:source "doi:10.1674/0003-0031(2000)144[0187:SBITBC]2.0.CO;2") oboInOwl:hasNarrowSynonym obo:ACTAN_0000929 "disruption sequence"@en)
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(dc:contributor "https://orcid.org/0000-0002-4277-2151") rdfs:label obo:ACTAN_0000929 "dynamically-unstable pattern")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(dc:source "doi:10.1111/brv.12891") skos:example obo:ACTAN_0000929 "\"Cicadas can drive bird predators out of forests both due to the dangerously loud and painful sound, and its disruption to their communication.\"")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(dc:source "doi:10.1002/ajp.23055") skos:example obo:ACTAN_0000929 "\"Saimiri sciureus (common squirrel monkey)...
encounters a challenge (a large gap between substrates), disrupting the footfall sequence...\"")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(dc:source "doi:10.1674/0003-0031(2000)144[0187:SBITBC]2.0.CO;2") skos:scopeNote obo:ACTAN_0000929 "\"Disruption of a spawning sequence also resulted if a male or female responded inappropriately to their mate.\"")
SubClassOf(obo:ACTAN_0000929 obo:ACTAN_0000064)
SubClassOf(obo:ACTAN_0000929 ObjectSomeValuesFrom(obo:RO_0000086 obo:PATO_0002026))

# Class: obo:ACTAN_0000930 (displacing relativity)

AnnotationAssertion(terms:conformsTo obo:ACTAN_0000930 <https://github.com/Active-Animals/Ontology/patterns/context_composite>)
AnnotationAssertion(oboInOwl:created_by obo:ACTAN_0000930 "Ditch Townsend")
AnnotationAssertion(oboInOwl:creation_date obo:ACTAN_0000930 "2025-11-18T09:03:25.007859Z")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(dc:source "doi:10.1674/0003-0031(2000)144[0187:SBITBC]2.0.CO;2") oboInOwl:hasDefinition obo:ACTAN_0000930 "Relativity which actively supplants another in its place.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(dc:date "1998"^^xsd:decimal) Annotation(dc:source "doi:10.1002/(SICI)1098-2337(1998)24:3<197::AID-AB4>3.0.CO;2-I") oboInOwl:hasExactSynonym obo:ACTAN_0000930 "displacing"@en)
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(dc:date "1967"^^xsd:decimal) Annotation(dc:source "https://open.uct.ac.za/handle/11427/13101") oboInOwl:hasExactSynonym obo:ACTAN_0000930 "supplanting")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(dc:date "1998"^^xsd:decimal) Annotation(dc:source "doi:10.1002/(SICI)1098-2337(1998)24:3<197::AID-AB4>3.0.CO;2-I") oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym obo:ACTAN_0000930 "expelling")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(dc:contributor "https://orcid.org/0000-0002-4277-2151") rdfs:label obo:ACTAN_0000930 "displacing relativity")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(dc:source "https://open.uct.ac.za/handle/11427/13101") skos:example obo:ACTAN_0000930 "\"A. ibis... 
Supplanting runs usually occur when two birds compete for individual food items, with one bird chasing another for one or two metres, and have also been observed in 20 - 30 day nestlings on the ground.\"")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(dc:source "doi:10.1674/0003-0031(2000)144[0187:SBITBC]2.0.CO;2") skos:example obo:ACTAN_0000930 "\"In Nocomis micropogon...
If the female’s snout moved aside or ahead of the male’s snout during their run, the male turned his head and displaced the female from the trough with a lateral head butt.\"")
SubClassOf(obo:ACTAN_0000930 obo:ACTAN_0000288)
SubClassOf(obo:ACTAN_0000930 ObjectSomeValuesFrom(obo:BFO_0000051 obo:ACTAN_0000385))

# Class: obo:ACTAN_0000931 (constriction squeeze)

AnnotationAssertion(terms:conformsTo obo:ACTAN_0000931 <https://github.com/Active-Animals/Ontology/patterns/sub_activity_by_quality>)
AnnotationAssertion(oboInOwl:created_by obo:ACTAN_0000931 "Ditch Townsend")
AnnotationAssertion(oboInOwl:creation_date obo:ACTAN_0000931 "2025-11-18T10:45:34.273435Z")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(dc:source "doi:10.1242/jeb.27.3.264") Annotation(dc:source "https://orcid.org/0000-0002-4277-2151") oboInOwl:hasDefinition obo:ACTAN_0000931 "Squeeze that involves a full-circle narrowing.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(dc:date "1950"^^xsd:decimal) Annotation(dc:source "doi:10.1242/jeb.27.3.264") oboInOwl:hasExactSynonym obo:ACTAN_0000931 "constriction"@en)
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(dc:contributor "https://orcid.org/0000-0002-4277-2151") rdfs:label obo:ACTAN_0000931 "constriction squeeze")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(dc:source "doi:10.1242/jeb.27.3.264") skos:example obo:ACTAN_0000931 "\"Metridium...
Constriction of the circular muscle fibre -narrows the column. When this happens the compressed coelenteric fluid enforces an extension of the longitudinal muscles of the column system.\"")
SubClassOf(obo:ACTAN_0000931 obo:ACTAN_0000845)
SubClassOf(obo:ACTAN_0000931 ObjectSomeValuesFrom(obo:RO_0000086 obo:PATO_0002239))

# Class: obo:ACTAN_0000932 (forelimb protraction)

AnnotationAssertion(terms:conformsTo obo:ACTAN_0000932 <https://github.com/Active-Animals/Ontology/patterns/sub_activity_by_entity>)
AnnotationAssertion(oboInOwl:created_by obo:ACTAN_0000932 "Ditch Townsend")
AnnotationAssertion(oboInOwl:creation_date obo:ACTAN_0000932 "2026-08-02T10:51:30.985815Z")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(dc:contributor "https://orcid.org/0000-0002-4277-2151") Annotation(rdfs:comment "Directly inferred.") oboInOwl:hasDefinition obo:ACTAN_0000932 "Protraction that results from forelimb protracting.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(dc:date "1992"^^xsd:decimal) Annotation(dc:source "doi:10.1002/ajpa.1330870108") Annotation(skos:scopeNote "\"...humerus was protracted...\"") oboInOwl:hasNarrowSynonym obo:ACTAN_0000932 "humerus protracted")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(dc:date "2019"^^xsd:decimal) Annotation(dc:source "doi:10.1002/ajp.23055") rdfs:label obo:ACTAN_0000932 "forelimb protraction"@en)
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(dc:source "doi:10.1111/jzo.12455") skos:example obo:ACTAN_0000932 "\"...it is likely that two-toed sloths are controlling their center of mass position through the mechanism... in which interlimb coordination is timed so that a protracted propulsive forelimb early in its support phase is synchronized with a retracted ipsilateral braking hind limb late in its support phase.\"")
SubClassOf(obo:ACTAN_0000932 obo:ACTAN_0000939)
SubClassOf(obo:ACTAN_0000932 ObjectSomeValuesFrom(obo:RO_0000057 obo:UBERON_0002102))

