# Class: obo:PATO_0002445 (torsioned)

AnnotationAssertion(obo:IAO_0000115 obo:PATO_0002445 "A shape quality inhering in a bearer by virtue of the bearer's being twisted or turned.")
AnnotationAssertion(terms:contributor obo:PATO_0002445 <https://orcid.org/0000-0002-2061-091X>)
AnnotationAssertion(oboInOwl:creation_date obo:PATO_0002445 "2013-01-29T11:05:26Z")
AnnotationAssertion(oboInOwl:hasExactSynonym obo:PATO_0002445 "twisted")
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:comment obo:PATO_0002445 "The word \"torsion\" has multiple different meanings in different context (e.g. the act of twisting or the morphology of the digestive tract in gastropods). This term refers purely to the resulting shape and is not to be used in the engineering and mechanics sense of torsion. 
Note: kinked PATO:0001798(synonym twisted) is similar to 'torsioned', but it is different in that something that is kinked has sharp twists or turns.")
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label obo:PATO_0002445 "torsioned")
SubClassOf(obo:PATO_0002445 obo:PATO_0000052)

