AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:comment obo:PO_0009001 "A fruit (PO:0009001) may contain additional plant structures (PO:0009011) that were part of a flower (PO:0009046) and mature along with the gynoecium, such as a receptacle (PO:0009064). A fruit may develop without fertilization in cases of parthenocarpy, apomixis, or other hormone-induced conditions and may not always contain seeds (PO:0009010). When annotating to fruit (PO:0009001) that are referred to as ‘multiple’, or ‘compound’, please annotate directly to the appropriate plant structure, such as receptacle, hypanthium (PO:0009065) or infructescence (PO:0006342). Fruits only occur in angiosperms.")
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label obo:PO_0009001 "fruit")
SubClassOf(obo:PO_0009001 obo:PO_0025496)
SubClassOf(obo:PO_0009001 obo:UBERON_0001062)

# Class: obo:PO_0009011 (plant structure)

AnnotationAssertion(oboInOwl:hasDefinition obo:PO_0009011 "Definition: A plant anatomical entity (PO:0025131) that is, or was, part of a plant, or was derived from a part of a plant.")
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:comment obo:PO_0009011 "'Part' includes both proper parts and the whole plant. CARO:0000003 'connected anatomical structure' is defined as: Material anatomical entity that is a single connected structure with inherent 3D shape, generated by coordinated expression of the organism's own genome.")
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label obo:PO_0009011 "plant structure")
SubClassOf(obo:PO_0009011 obo:PO_0025131)

# Class: obo:PO_0025131 (plant anatomical entity)

AnnotationAssertion(oboInOwl:created_by obo:PO_0025131 "rwalls")
AnnotationAssertion(oboInOwl:creation_date obo:PO_0025131 "2010-11-15T11:41:38Z")
AnnotationAssertion(oboInOwl:hasDefinition obo:PO_0025131 "Definition: An anatomical entity that is or was part of a plant.")
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:comment obo:PO_0025131 "Includes both material entities such as plant structures and immaterial entities such as plant anatomical spaces. CARO:0000000 'anatomical entity' is defined as: A part of a cellular organism that is either an immaterial entity or a material entity with granularity aboove the level of a protein complex.  Or, a substance produced by a cellular organism with granularity above the level of a protein complex.  Refers to BFO:0000004 'independent continuant'.")
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label obo:PO_0025131 "plant anatomical entity")
SubClassOf(obo:PO_0025131 obo:BFO_0000040)

# Class: obo:PO_0025496 (multi-tissue plant structure)

AnnotationAssertion(oboInOwl:created_by obo:PO_0025496 "Laurel_Cooper")
AnnotationAssertion(oboInOwl:creation_date obo:PO_0025496 "2012-06-11T14:57:00Z")
AnnotationAssertion(oboInOwl:hasDefinition obo:PO_0025496 "Definition: A plant structure (PO:0009011) that has as parts two or more portions of plant tissue (PO:0009007) of at least two different types and which through specific morphogenetic processes forms a single structural unit demarcated by primarily bona-fide boundaries from other structural units of different types.")
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:comment obo:PO_0025496 "Most multi-tissue plant structures have at least a small connection to other plant structures via a fiat boundary, such as where a leaf (PO:0025034) connects to a shoot axis (PO:0025029), a petal (PO:0009032) connects to a receptacle (PO:0009064), or a branch (PO:0025073) connects to a stem (PO:0009047).  Refers to CARO:0000055 multi-tissue structure, def'n: Anatomical structure that has as parts two or more portions of tissue of at least two different types, and which through specific morphogenetic processes, form a single distinct structural unit demarcated by bona-fide boundries from other structural units of differnt types.")
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label obo:PO_0025496 "multi-tissue plant structure")
SubClassOf(obo:PO_0025496 obo:PO_0009011)

# Class: obo:UBERON_0000004 (nose)

AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref "UBERON:cjm") obo:IAO_0000115 obo:UBERON_0000004 "The olfactory organ of vertebrates, consisting of nares, olfactory epithelia and the structures and skeletal framework of the nasal cavity.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(oboInOwl:source "ZFA:0000047") obo:UBPROP_0000001 obo:UBERON_0000004 "Organ that is the specialized structure of the face that contains olfactory neurons. The peripheral olfactory organ is paired[ZFA:0000047].")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(oboInOwl:source "Wikipedia:Nose") obo:UBPROP_0000001 obo:UBERON_0000004 "a protuberance in vertebrates that houses the nostrils, or nares, which admit and expel air for respiration in conjunction with the mouth. Behind the nose are the olfactory mucosa and the sinuses. Behind the nasal cavity, air next passes through the pharynx, shared with the digestive system, and then into the rest of the respiratory system. In humans, the nose is located centrally on the face; on most other mammals, it is on the upper tip of the snout[WP]. GO: The nose is the specialized structure of the face that serves as the organ of the sense of smell and as part of the respiratory system. Includes the nasi externus (external nose) and cavitas nasi (nasal cavity)[Wikipedia:Nose].")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(oboInOwl:source "MP:0002233") obo:UBPROP_0000001 obo:UBERON_0000004 "the organ that is specialized for smell and is part of the respiratory system")
AnnotationAssertion(obo:UBPROP_0000008 obo:UBERON_0000004 "the structure of the nose varies across vertebrates. In tetrapods the nose is part of the respiratory system.[PMID:25312359]")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref "ZFA:0000047") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasSynonymType <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/uberon/core#SENSU>) oboInOwl:hasExactSynonym obo:UBERON_0000004 "nasal sac")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref "MA:0000281") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasSynonymType <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/uberon/core#HUMAN_PREFERRED>) oboInOwl:hasExactSynonym obo:UBERON_0000004 "nose")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref "ZFA:0000047") oboInOwl:hasExactSynonym obo:UBERON_0000004 "peripheral olfactory organ")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref "Wikipedia:Nose") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasSynonymType obo:OMO_0003011) oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym obo:UBERON_0000004 "nasus")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref "UBERON:cjm") oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym obo:UBERON_0000004 "olfactory apparatus")
AnnotationAssertion(oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym obo:UBERON_0000004 "proboscis")
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label obo:UBERON_0000004 "nose")
SubClassOf(obo:UBERON_0000004 obo:UBERON_0001456)

# Class: obo:UBERON_0000015 (non-material anatomical boundary)

AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref "CARO:0000010") obo:IAO_0000115 obo:UBERON_0000015 "A non-material anatomical entity of two dimensions. Anatomical boundaries are contiguous structures.")
AnnotationAssertion(obo:RO_0002175 obo:UBERON_0000015 obo:NCBITaxon_33208)
AnnotationAssertion(obo:RO_0002175 obo:UBERON_0000015 obo:NCBITaxon_4751)
AnnotationAssertion(oboInOwl:hasDbXref obo:UBERON_0000015 "AEO:0000192")
AnnotationAssertion(oboInOwl:hasDbXref obo:UBERON_0000015 "CARO:0000010")
AnnotationAssertion(oboInOwl:hasDbXref obo:UBERON_0000015 "FMA:50705")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref "CARO:0000010") oboInOwl:hasExactSynonym obo:UBERON_0000015 "anatomical boundary")
AnnotationAssertion(oboInOwl:id obo:UBERON_0000015 "UBERON:0000015")
AnnotationAssertion(oboInOwl:inSubset obo:UBERON_0000015 <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/uberon/core#common_anatomy>)
AnnotationAssertion(oboInOwl:inSubset obo:UBERON_0000015 <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/uberon/core#human_subset>)
AnnotationAssertion(oboInOwl:inSubset obo:UBERON_0000015 <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/uberon/core#mouse_subset>)
AnnotationAssertion(oboInOwl:inSubset obo:UBERON_0000015 <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/uberon/core#upper_level>)
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:comment obo:UBERON_0000015 "Except in the case of abstracted fiat boundaries such as the midline plane of an organism, all 2D anatomical entities have a 3 dimensional projection. For example, the surface of the shell of a muscle has a distinct shape that projects into the third dimension. Note that boundaries are 2D structures. They have no thickness - and so can not be sites of gene expression or gene product localisation. For this, use boundary region terms.")
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label obo:UBERON_0000015 "non-material anatomical boundary")
SubClassOf(Annotation(oboInOwl:source "CARO") obo:UBERON_0000015 obo:UBERON_0000466)

# Class: obo:UBERON_0000020 (sense organ)

AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref "https://github.com/obophenotype/uberon/issues/549") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref "https://orcid.org/0000-0002-6601-2165") obo:IAO_0000115 obo:UBERON_0000020 "An organ that is capable of transducing sensory stimulus to the nervous system.")
AnnotationAssertion(dc:contributor obo:UBERON_0000020 <https://github.com/cmungall>)
